...is that the *rearrangement* of the _existing_ boulders *plus* the
_added_ boulders from the giants can certainly be a serious problem.
A maximum negative luck is nothing a proficient player will accept to
achieve; it's too risky, even if there happens to be an altar (which
is not something you can assume, as already said).

Fixing a really lot of luck loss from the many many rearranged boulders
would be a serious problem as explained by other posters, and usually
one wouldn't finish Sokoban then for exactly that reason in most cases.

In my games, luckily, giants never appeared early in a Sokoban, rather
only when most boulders have already been at their final destination,
so that was practically never a problem. But I don't want to imagine if
they'd come early and spoil the level. Missing all the wands and rings
can be a serious disadvantage, or, alternatively, any huge negative luck
a significant problem.

